# Sample .worktreeinclude for the repository root. Project setup writes one itself and keeps its list between
# "# benchkeeper:worktrees" markers; lines outside them are yours.
# One literal path per line, relative to the repository root; no wildcards, no negations, no leading slash.
# Orca copies the entries from the primary checkout into each new worktree, only when they exist and Git ignores them
# (a local setup lists them in .git/info/exclude). Claude Code reads the same file as .gitignore patterns.
CLAUDE.local.md
AGENTS.override.md
.claude/settings.local.json
.claude/hooks/benchkeeper-guard.mjs
.benchkeeper/state.json
skills-lock.json
.claude/skills
.agents/skills
.worktreeinclude
